<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!--
  Regolith surface for the Lunabotics arena.

  Squeezed from the original 26 x 30.5 m footprint down to the 9.44 x 8.40 m
  outer footprint of the UCF regolith bin (the 9.14 x 8.10 m bed plus the
  0.15 m wall on each side, so the terrain tucks under the walls with no gap),
  and re-centred on the bed, whose centre is (0, 4.05) in the guidebook Origin
  Point frame.

  Three things about gz heightmaps that this file depends on, all confirmed by
  dropping probe bodies onto the terrain in gz-sim (Jazzy / gz-sim 8):

  1. <pos> is NOT applied to the collision heightmap - only the visual honours
     it, so a <pos> offset silently puts the collision terrain somewhere the
     visual terrain is not.  Both <pos> values are therefore left at zero and
     the whole offset lives in the model <pose>, which both honour.

  2. The rendered footprint comes out at (n-1)/n of the requested <size>, with
     n = 33 samples for this DEM.  9.735 x 8.663 x 32/33 = 9.44 x 8.40 m.

  3. The third <size> component scales the relief linearly: the surface ends up
     at minElevation + normalisedHeight * size_z, i.e. spanning size_z metres
     from the DEM's low point.  moon.tif has minElevation = -212.296 m, so the
     model <pose> Z of 212.084 puts the mean surface height at world z = 0
     (surface range -0.21 m to +0.09 m).

  size_z was 1 before the squeeze.  Kept at 1 it would put a 1 m dune inside a
  9 m competition bin, so it is dropped to 0.30 for a gently undulating bed;
  the guidebook's craters and boulders are the real relief.  If you change it,
  move the <pose> Z with it to keep grade at zero: pose_z = 212.296 - 0.707 * size_z.

  Note: the 40-50 cm craters of guidebook section 3.1 are NOT modelled.
  moon.tif is only 33 x 33 samples, i.e. ~0.29 x 0.25 m per cell at this size,
  so a crater would be two cells wide - adding them means replacing the raster.
-->
<sdf version="1.9">
  <model name="moon">
    <static>true</static>
    <pose>0 4.05 212.084 0 0 0</pose>
    <link name="link">
      <collision name="collision">
        <geometry>
          <heightmap>
            <uri>dem/moon.tif</uri>
            <size>9.735 8.663 0.30</size>
            <pos>0 0 0</pos>
          </heightmap>
        </geometry>
      </collision>
      <visual name="visual">
        <geometry>
          <heightmap>
            <use_terrain_paging>false</use_terrain_paging>
            <texture>
              <diffuse>materials/textures/sand.jpg</diffuse>
              <normal>materials/textures/moon_normal.png</normal>
              <size>2</size>
            </texture>
            <uri>dem/moon.tif</uri>
            <size>9.735 8.663 0.30</size>
            <pos>0 0 0</pos>
            <sampling>2</sampling> <!-- Sampling rate for the heightmap -->
          </heightmap>
        </geometry>
      </visual>
    </link>
  </model>
</sdf>
